  "note": "Election of the Dungannon Urban District Council, Wednesday 18 May 1955 (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1955, p. 6, 'Ulster municipal nominations'); no ward was contested. 'Fourteen Unionists have been returned unopposed for the East and Central Wards' - no label is printed against the individual names. Patton, Dickie, Dickson, Walker and Brown were newcomers. All seven names confirmed on the block image of the cited article (BNL19550505.2.142); the OCR reads Patton as 'K. J. F. Patton' and M'Crea as M'Crca. Returned unopposed."
